# No emdashes

Do not use the emdash character (`—`) or en dash (`–`) in user-facing marketing copy, UI strings, metadata descriptions, or comments that mirror product voice.

Prefer commas, periods, colons, or a short rewrite instead.

Examples:
- Bad: `One link — no domain stress.`
- Good: `One link. No domain stress.`
- Good: `One link: no domain stress.`
